   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Week 7 – Outlier Detection and Removal (IQR Method)\n",
    "\n",
    "The final step before Tableau is handling **statistical outliers** -> values that are technically valid (not zero, not negative) but extreme enough to distort market averages and trend lines.\n",
    "\n",
    "Consistent with the strategy from Weeks 4–5, outlier records are **flagged, not deleted**. The flagged file keeps everything. A separate Tableau-ready file applies the filter. This way the raw data is always preserved for reference.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Fields filtered\n",
    "| Field | Rationale |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `ClosePrice` | Remove extreme low/high sales that distort median trends |\n",
    "| `LivingArea` | Remove implausible square footage (17M sq ft, zeros already caught) |\n",
    "| `DaysOnMarket` | Remove the 12,430-day records while keeping legitimately slow sales |\n",
    "| `price_per_sqft` | Derived metric — outliers here usually reflect bad LivingArea data |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "fb720706",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded — Sold: 413,561 rows  |  Listing: 549,460 rows\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "\n",
    "sold    = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(OUTPUT_PATH, \"sold_features.csv\"),    low_memory=False)\n",
    "listing = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(OUTPUT_PATH, \"listing_features.csv\"), low_memory=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in [\"CloseDate\",\"ListingContractDate\",\"PurchaseContractDate\"]:\n",
    "    for df in [sold, listing]:\n",
    "        if col in df.columns:\n",
    "            df[col] = pd.to_datetime(df[col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded — Sold: {len(sold):,} rows  |  Listing: {len(listing):,} rows\")"
   ]
  },
